WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.578
In the original a Nightmare on Elm Street.

00:00:01.594 --> 00:00:04.186
Those who are looking out for it will notice a clue in the nightmare scenes

00:00:04.218 --> 00:00:05.930
that indicate that the character is dreaming.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.826
If you see the red and green stripe pattern, similar to Freddy's iconic sweater,

00:00:08.858 --> 00:00:11.070
you know you're in for a bad time.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.286
The second movie, Freddy's Revenge, spends less time in the dream world with

00:00:14.308 --> 00:00:17.006
Freddy's new approach being to take control of someone in the real world to

00:00:17.028 --> 00:00:17.674
do his bidding.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:20.894
But if you're looking for it, green and red are still used to signify his

00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:23.818
reign of terror, this time using lights and set design elements.

00:00:23.914 --> 00:00:27.206
When Jesse sneaks out to the bar, Don's Place, it's illuminated in red and green,

00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:28.402
alternating lights.

00:00:28.466 --> 00:00:31.958
The ensuing gym and shower scene also features hues of red and green.

00:00:32.044 --> 00:00:35.218
Jesse and Lisa share a moment together in the pool house where Freddy starts

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.262
to take over Jesse's body and the towels hanging behind them are a green

00:00:38.316 --> 00:00:40.162
striped towel and a red striped towel.

00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:43.174
There's a similar attack in Grady's room, which is covered in wallpaper

00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:44.950
featuring red and green shapes.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.382
Lisa's pool party is crashed by Freddy Krueger.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:50.186
The brick perimeter and the rest of the backyard are covered in red and green

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.086
alternating uplights, which are most visible.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.702
As Freddy takes control of the party.

00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:57.194
As he causes mayhem in the house, the TV glows red and the mirror glows green.

00:00:57.242 --> 00:01:00.942
Finally, the finale at the abandoned power plant defies logic because

00:01:00.996 --> 00:01:04.526
there wouldn't be lights on in an abandoned plant, but the place is lit up

00:01:04.548 --> 00:01:05.818
with reds and greens.

00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:08.626
The impressive part is how they manage to do all of this without making it

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:10.130
feel too Christmassy.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:12.763
🎵Christmas Music🎵

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:16.498
To learn about all of Nightmare Two's secrets, stick around to the end of

00:01:16.504 --> 00:01:17.300
this video.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.954
🎵Metal Music🎵

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.678
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:24.866
The Revenge.

00:01:24.978 --> 00:01:27.878
After directing the first Nightmare on Elm Street, Wes Craven was given the

00:01:27.884 --> 00:01:29.314
opportunity to direct the sequel.

00:01:29.362 --> 00:01:30.994
Craven never really wanted a sequel.

00:01:31.042 --> 00:01:33.894
In fact, the ending of the first one where Freddy takes over the convertible

00:01:33.942 --> 00:01:35.210
was done against his will.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.798
Still, he agreed to read the script for A Nightmare on Elm Street 2.

00:01:37.814 --> 00:01:41.434
Didn't like the concept or the scene with the exploding parakeets and

00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:43.894
turned his focus back to the Hills Have Eyes franchise.

00:01:44.022 --> 00:01:47.454
This guy, Jack Shoulder, took the directing job and apparently was so

00:01:47.492 --> 00:01:51.086
focused on fulfilling his duties that he didn't notice this subtext going on

00:01:51.108 --> 00:01:51.722
in the script.

00:01:51.786 --> 00:01:55.934
-[Jack] I never really thought a whole lot about the underlying stuff that was going on.

00:01:55.972 --> 00:01:59.314
-[Jack] All the talk about the gay theme, it never occurred to me.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:03.966
-[Jack] I was just trying to make my days and get this complicated thing shot.

00:02:04.078 --> 00:02:07.374
A lot of these were pretty blatant when you watch the film, thanks to shots

00:02:07.422 --> 00:02:09.698
like this or lines like this.

00:02:09.864 --> 00:02:12.190
-[Jesse] Something is trying to get inside my body.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.818
-[Grady] Yeah, and she's female and she's waiting for you in the cabana and you want to sleep with me.

00:02:15.818 --> 00:02:17.754
But there are a few things I noticed that I haven't seen

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:18.618
anyone talk about.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.260
So let's cut in to the Things You Missed.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.730
(Slice)

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.427
🎵Mysterious Music🎵

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:29.254
The opening scene takes place in a nightmare where the main character,

00:02:29.302 --> 00:02:32.022
Jesse, is trapped on a school bus operated by Freddy Krueger.

00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:34.894
At the beginning of the dream, the driver can be seen and identified as

00:02:34.932 --> 00:02:38.186
Robert England, the Freddy actor, out of makeup, something I didn't realize

00:02:38.218 --> 00:02:39.804
until after seeing New Nightmare. 

00:02:39.804 --> 00:02:42.234
On the bus dashboard, there's also a body glove sticker.

00:02:42.282 --> 00:02:43.594
Bodyglove is a surfing brand.

00:02:43.642 --> 00:02:46.074
And as I mentioned in The Things You Missed episode on the first movie,

00:02:46.122 --> 00:02:49.326
Robert England was really into surfing and even acted in a surfing movie

00:02:49.358 --> 00:02:50.270
called Big Wednesday.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.914
So this sticker is probably a little nod to that.

00:02:53.032 --> 00:02:55.998
Five years have passed since the first movie and the Walsh family has moved

00:02:56.014 --> 00:02:58.254
into the house once occupied by Nancy Thompson.

00:02:58.302 --> 00:03:01.766
The bars have only been removed from the bottom floor, which makes no sense.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.742
Jesse is a teenage student who attends the local Springwood high school

00:03:04.796 --> 00:03:07.318
which, by the way, is the first mention of the town by name.

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:10.346
It's not in the first movie, so Springwood was actually an invention of the

00:03:10.368 --> 00:03:11.734
screenwriter David Chaskin.

00:03:11.782 --> 00:03:15.174
He's the one responsible for the LGBT themes in the subtext of the movie,

00:03:15.222 --> 00:03:16.922
and I think this is the first example.

00:03:17.056 --> 00:03:20.130
Like Springwood... Springwood.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.978
Jesse also pulls up next to this car with the

00:03:21.984 --> 00:03:23.822
rainbow stickers every time in the parking lot.

00:03:23.876 --> 00:03:26.986
There's this whole pantsing ordeal in gym class between Jesse and Grady,

00:03:27.018 --> 00:03:30.897
who's implied to be Jesse's crush, and the coach tells them this

00:03:30.897 --> 00:03:32.318
 -[Coach] Assume the position

00:03:32.324 --> 00:03:35.150
I don't know if they're supposed to be doing pushups or planks, but either way,

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.046
terrible form.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:38.994
They use this time to gossip about the gym teacher, which comes into play

00:03:39.032 --> 00:03:39.620
later.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.811
-[Grady] Guy gets his rocks off like this.  

00:03:41.811 --> 00:03:43.951
-[Grady] Hangs around queer S&amp;M joints downtown. 

00:03:43.951 --> 00:03:45.717
-[Grady] He likes pretty boys like you.

00:03:45.717 --> 00:03:47.784
For the first movie, I talked about how Freddy represents

00:03:47.784 --> 00:03:49.985
the strained relationship between Nancy and her mom.

00:03:49.985 --> 00:03:52.694
But in this one, he plays by different rules and has a different

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.554
meaning for the film.

00:03:53.602 --> 00:03:56.774
He's trying to take over Jesse's body and use him to kill people in the real world.

00:03:56.812 --> 00:04:00.246
Jesse realizes what's going on and tries to hide and repress his problem.

00:04:00.268 --> 00:04:03.234
It's the opposite of Nancy's situation in the first one.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.206
She wanted her parents to believe her about Freddy,

00:04:05.238 --> 00:04:08.905
whereas Jesse refuses his parents help and tries to deal with things on his own.

00:04:08.905 --> 00:04:12.026
It represents his closeted homosexuality, which we see clues of

00:04:12.048 --> 00:04:14.922
throughout the movie, like his flamboyant dancing while cleaning his room.

00:04:14.976 --> 00:04:17.838
Notice how he's embarrassed when someone else sees his moves and tries to

00:04:17.844 --> 00:04:18.526
hide everything.

00:04:18.628 --> 00:04:22.042
The sign on his door says, no out of town chicks, which from a distance

00:04:22.106 --> 00:04:23.450
reads as no chicks.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.318
And he literally has a game called Probe hidden in his closet.

00:04:26.414 --> 00:04:29.010
Whenever he wakes up from a nightmare, he screams like a girl.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.340
An example of him literally letting his true nature out in the open.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.906
As I mentioned, much of Jesse's repressed sexuality is connected to the gym

00:04:39.938 --> 00:04:41.058
teacher, Coach Schneider.

00:04:41.154 --> 00:04:44.614
After class one day, Jesse is punished when the coach hears him say this

00:04:44.732 --> 00:04:46.710
-[Jesse] Schneider's always got a stick up his !@#

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:51.766
Is he speaking metaphorically or literally? That night, Jesse visits the

00:04:51.788 --> 00:04:54.986
aforementioned S&amp;M joint that Coach Schneider frequents and somehow just

00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:59.194
walks into a 21 plus bar and orders a beer without being ID or asked to pay

00:04:59.232 --> 00:04:59.696
for it.

00:04:59.696 --> 00:05:02.486
The bartender is actually a cameo from a Nightmare on Elm Street series

00:05:02.518 --> 00:05:06.014
producer Robert Shea, but Jesse is caught when the coach recognizes him and

00:05:06.052 --> 00:05:09.210
taken back to the school to run laps, which is also pretty weird.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.850
The ensuing scene is filled with S&amp;M themes.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.878
Coach Schneider grabs a jump rope, which later comes to life and ties his

00:05:14.884 --> 00:05:17.978
hands above his head, which creates a very specific image considering he's

00:05:17.994 --> 00:05:19.810
still wearing his S&amp;M gear from the bar.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.878
Side note, the jump rope also ties into the nursery rhyme about Freddy Krueger,

00:05:22.894 --> 00:05:26.194
which is often recited by a group of jump roping little kids.

00:05:26.232 --> 00:05:29.086
Like when Jessie goes into his sister's room the next night and sees her jump roping.

00:05:29.118 --> 00:05:30.882
And also, she has no bed.

00:05:30.936 --> 00:05:33.970
Where does she sleep? Does she just throw herself onto the stuffed animals?

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.778
She does have a bed in a different scene.

00:05:35.874 --> 00:05:38.806
I'm guessing they just didn't have room for the jump rope and the bed and

00:05:38.828 --> 00:05:40.646
just decided, we'll pull the bed out for this one.

00:05:40.668 --> 00:05:42.470
I'm sure nobody will notice anyway.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:45.706
We also see a picture of a kid jump roping in the kitchen, suggesting that

00:05:45.728 --> 00:05:48.502
all of these strange scenes are linked to the legend of Freddy Krueger.

00:05:48.566 --> 00:05:50.892
Back to Jesse's weird underage drinking punishment.

00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:55.226
 He's told to hit the showers. And these showerheads look very much like something else, much like

00:05:55.248 --> 00:05:56.730
the showerheads seen in Carrie.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:59.326
As Coach Schneider is getting pulled through the locker room by some

00:05:59.348 --> 00:06:02.958
supernatural force, we see this dirty towel sign partially obstructed by the wall,

00:06:02.964 --> 00:06:05.850
almost making it look like it's pointing out the coach as dirty,

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.938
similar to the no chicks sign in Jesse's room.

00:06:08.024 --> 00:06:11.294
When Freddy appears, he scratches the coach's back with his claw, possibly

00:06:11.342 --> 00:06:13.406
another reference to his S&amp;M practices.

00:06:13.518 --> 00:06:17.054
But the movie seems to imply that Jesse really did this, because afterwards

00:06:17.102 --> 00:06:19.118
we see him wearing the iconic glove.

00:06:19.214 --> 00:06:21.846
The next day, there's a scene where the dad is removing the bars from the

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:25.334
top floor, and there's this very weird shot of the parents arguing about

00:06:25.372 --> 00:06:26.594
what should be done about Jesse.

00:06:26.642 --> 00:06:29.706
I know the director said that he wasn't aware of any of the subtext in the

00:06:29.728 --> 00:06:33.738
script, but yeah, I don't know.

00:06:33.824 --> 00:06:36.806
Later that week, Jesse's friend Lisa celebrates her birthday with

00:06:36.838 --> 00:06:37.610
 a pool party.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.166
Dude, why did you install a diving board in your pool if you don't want

00:06:45.188 --> 00:06:48.474
people to use it? Jesse finds himself alone in the pool house with Lisa,

00:06:48.522 --> 00:06:51.008
who's crushing on him, and this is his response

00:06:51.008 --> 00:06:51.854
-[Jesse] I'm gonna leave.

00:06:51.892 --> 00:06:53.006
-[Jesse[ I'm not into this.

00:06:53.108 --> 00:06:53.614
Uh, wow.

00:06:53.652 --> 00:06:54.350
You don't say.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:58.286
-[Jesse] How can you help me?

00:06:58.286 --> 00:06:59.442
Yeah, she's not getting it.

00:06:59.496 --> 00:07:02.526
She ends up trying to get busy with him and probably not wanting to expose

00:07:02.558 --> 00:07:03.890
his secret, he plays along.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.102
But to his horror, this huge, rotting tongue comes out of his mouth.

00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:10.534
And after realizing it, he gets dressed and proceeds to go to Grady's house,

00:07:10.572 --> 00:07:12.022
where he asks to stay over with him.

00:07:12.076 --> 00:07:15.766
He's trying to keep his Freddy problem, or metaphorically his sexuality, a

00:07:15.788 --> 00:07:17.990
secret because he feels ashamed of admitting it.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.978
But it's spilling out into the open in ways that he did not intend.

00:07:21.074 --> 00:07:24.294
He refers to it as something inside of him which could refer to him bottling

00:07:24.342 --> 00:07:27.754
up his feelings towards Grady or the more literal idea of Freddy getting

00:07:27.792 --> 00:07:30.282
inside of him and controlling him to do horrible things.

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:33.706
Going to Grady's ends up being a bad idea because it just causes Freddy to

00:07:33.728 --> 00:07:35.898
emerge again and Grady is the next victim.

00:07:35.994 --> 00:07:39.342
After his death, Jesse looks into the mirror and sees Freddy standing there.

00:07:39.396 --> 00:07:43.453
When he says, you son of a you killed him, I think he's really talking about himself, 

00:07:43.453 --> 00:07:45.534
frustrated with these feelings that he can't control.

00:07:45.652 --> 00:07:48.706
To make matters worse, back at the party, everyone there has coupled off

00:07:48.728 --> 00:07:51.662
with someone of the opposite sex, making Jesse feel even more alone.

00:07:51.726 --> 00:07:54.958
Lisa still hasn't given up on him, though, even when he comes back covered

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:55.518
in blood.

00:07:55.614 --> 00:07:57.764
-[Lisa] What happened?

00:07:57.764 --> 00:07:59.230
-[Jesse] I killed Grady.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:01.450
-[Jesse] Lisa. I killed Schneider.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:06.722
-[Lisa] It's gotta be everything you've taken in Schneider, the diary, the glove.

00:08:06.866 --> 00:08:09.506
Yeah. Apparently, if a girl likes you enough, you can just start killing

00:08:09.538 --> 00:08:11.762
people and she'll still make up excuses for you.

00:08:11.836 --> 00:08:14.730
Even after Freddy takes over again and tries to kill her.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.946
It's only after Lisa confesses her love towards him that she's able to

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:20.042
damage Freddy and ultimately defeat him.

00:08:20.096 --> 00:08:23.126
Jesse goes back to school and seems to be romantically involved with Lisa now.

00:08:23.158 --> 00:08:26.346
My perception of the ending is that Jesse was able to see the negative

00:08:26.378 --> 00:08:28.270
effects of what would happen if he came out.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.854
In a literal sense, it's Freddy Krueger taking over and causing him shame by

00:08:31.892 --> 00:08:32.750
making him kill people.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.646
But in a metaphorical sense, it's the shame that he feels about his own

00:08:35.668 --> 00:08:38.142
desires and how he'll be perceived if he follows them.

00:08:38.196 --> 00:08:40.094
In that sense, it's kind of a sad ending.

00:08:40.142 --> 00:08:42.782
Much like the first movie, this was kind of a short episode.

00:08:42.846 --> 00:08:45.266
There aren't that many things you might have missed because by the

00:08:45.288 --> 00:08:48.110
director's own admission, he wasn't really thinking about subtext.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.362
-[Jack] I was just trying to get this complicated thing shot.

00:08:51.426 --> 00:08:54.086
So almost everything we talked about in this one is stuff that was in the script.

00:08:54.108 --> 00:08:57.394
The good news is that this one has probably the coolest logo

00:08:57.442 --> 00:08:58.278
animation ever.

00:08:58.364 --> 00:08:59.240
It's amazing.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.002
And if you watch this movie, then I've got news for you.

00:09:03.056 --> 00:09:03.894
You are now gay.

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:05.018
And I know what you're thinking.

00:09:05.104 --> 00:09:09.418
CZ didn't you have to watch the movie in order to make this video? Well, no.

00:09:09.504 --> 00:09:12.954
What I did is I actually set up a mirror in front of my computer and I only

00:09:12.992 --> 00:09:15.182
saw the movie through that, so technically, I'm good.

00:09:15.236 --> 00:09:19.647
Not that there's anything wrong with being gay, but I just decided to stay straight.

00:09:19.648 --> 00:09:21.151
(laughter)

00:09:21.151 --> 00:09:23.678
If you want to watch the next episode of Things You Missed on

00:09:23.684 --> 00:09:26.926
Nightmare Three, click that video on the left, and if you don't click it,

00:09:26.948 --> 00:09:28.350
then you will explode.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.382
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:09:32.436 --> 00:09:35.734
Ring the Deathbell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one,

00:09:35.772 --> 00:09:38.230
assuming we both survive.

